I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is the node's entire authority. The approval note says the graph definition hasn't been updated yet, and the fetch would send digest text to an external host. The node below imports only the notifier. Once the graph's `with` clause is updated, the http-client import can be added.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        let message = format!("Digest {}: {}", composed.date, composed.overview);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
